  1201	On the fourth day he went up the market steps without the stick, slowly, with his hand on the rail and his knees giving him their opinion of every tread. At the top he stood in the cold square by the pump and waited to see whether they would let him come down again. They did. He went down and up a second time to be sure, and an old woman shelling the last of somebody's dried beans on the wall watched him do it with deep suspicion, as if he were practising to steal something.
