  1277	He learned things in that hour that he could not have learned in a year of benches. He learned that the hold had a texture. When it was new it was soft at the very start, like a hand closing, and only then hard. When it had seen a thing three times it was hard from the first touch, like a door already shut. He learned that the recovery had a texture too. If he hit in it, before the next low breath, the arm he hit was only an arm, and it gave, and it was warm, and he could feel the man's pulse in it. And he learned that every one of these things cost him. He had always known a map of a man who hit back would be bought with bruises. He had not known how many.
