  1501	It was a week to the day since the main floor, a Tuesday again, grey and very cold, with a skin of ice on the water barrel by the side door that the night man had broken with his heel. They had the alcove to themselves for two hours before the sweepers. Brom had hung the lamp, and taken his coat off, and stood on his cross and said nothing at all, not even *what are you testing*, because Cael had told him on the walk down from the corner. *All of it. What you are when you're not being kind.*
