  1795	
  1796	"No crosses today," he said. "Nobody's hitting anybody. You're going to stand there, or sit, whatever you like, and try to find me with it. I'm going to make it easy." He did something then that Cael could not see, and did not need to see. "I'm as loud as I go. I'm standing here with the read open all the way and nothing else in my head. If you can't hear me now, you won't hear anybody."
  1797	
  1798	"And you'll watch."
  1799	
  1800	"I'll watch you not be able to." Brom said it without unkindness, as a plain forecast, like weather. "Then I'll tell you why. I've had two years with mine. I'm the only person in this city who knows what it's meant to feel like from the inside, and I'll be honest with you: I don't know how to say it. Nobody ever had to say it to me." He moved his shoulders. "So I'll watch, and when I see what you're doing wrong I'll try to find a word for it."
  1801	
