  1868	It was a small movement, nothing, a big man settling. But Cael's attention went to it. It went the way it had been trained to go, toward the movement, quick, to find out what it meant; and the moment it went, it was aiming, and the fire at his back was gone, and he was sitting on a cold floor in a lamplit alcove with his eyes wide open and his heart going like a hammer.
